# Baby Tracker — Cursor Rules (legacy pointer)

Rules have moved to `.cursor/rules/*.mdc` — Cursor loads them automatically by file context.
This file is kept only so older Cursor versions have a fallback.

## Core (always applies)

See `.cursor/rules/core.mdc` for the full mandatory workflow.

- ONE milestone per session. Complete it, hand off, STOP. No self-chaining.
- 3-strike rule: max 3 fix attempts in scoped files → `bugs/bug_<id>.md` → stop.
- Never hardcode secrets. Never commit `.env` or credential JSON.
- Commits are human-only.
- Mandatory handoff always: `baby-tracker-handoff` skill before stopping.
- Plan write-off: mark milestones ✅ in `plans/` only after human approves post-review (`milestone N approved` / `mark M[N] complete`).
- Commits: invoke **`safe-commit-push`** (worktree-aware; warns if localhost:3000 won't update).

## Architecture (non-negotiable)

- Frontend: `src/App.tsx` only. No `components/` dir unless a plan calls for it.
- Types: `src/types.ts` only.
- DB: `server/db.ts` only. No Firestore in `server.ts` or `src/`.
- Routes: `server.ts` only.
- Hebrew UI strings; English code and comments.

## Other rules — auto-loaded by file context

| Open file | Rule file loaded |
|-----------|-----------------|
| `server/db.ts` or `src/types.ts` | `.cursor/rules/db-rules.mdc` |
| `server.ts` | `.cursor/rules/server-rules.mdc` |
| `src/App.tsx`, `src/index.css` | `.cursor/rules/frontend-rules.mdc` |
| Adding a feature or checking scope | `.cursor/rules/feature-guide.mdc` |
| After any change, before handoff | `.cursor/rules/testing.mdc` |
